{
  "id": "pfjkppv",
  "title": "CHAPTER 12: PRACTICE QUESTIONS – MADHYA PRADESH GK",
  "order": 13,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "ncvjk2x",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "12.1 Multiple Choice Questions – History"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "1. Madhya Pradesh was formed on which date?",
      "id": "jxvy567"
    },
    {
      "id": "c5c5rmd",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "A) 15 August 1947",
        "B) 26 January 1950",
        "C) 1 November 1956",
        "D) 1 November 2000"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "<strong>Answer: C - 1 November 1956 (MP Foundation Day)</strong>",
      "id": "rqoa0j9"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "2. The Bhimbetka Rock Shelters were discovered by:",
      "id": "h3h78t7"
    },
    {
      "id": "dfv7gjh",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "A) D.R. Bhandarkar",
        "B) V.S. Wakankar",
        "C) John Marshall",
        "D) Alexander Cunningham"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "<strong>Answer: B - V.S. Wakankar (in 1957-58)</strong>",
      "id": "7whw2wu"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "3. Sanchi Stupa was originally built by:",
      "id": "ly3h3pq"
    },
    {
      "id": "so84ir5",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "A) Harsha",
        "B) Chandragupta Maurya",
        "C) Emperor Ashoka",
        "D) Samudragupta"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "<strong>Answer: C - Emperor Ashoka</strong>",
      "id": "m34mf4s"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "4. The famous Tansen, one of the Navratnas of Akbar, was born in:",
      "id": "wa4c1lq"
    },
    {
      "id": "iv4zpqx",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "A) Agra",
        "B) Gwalior",
        "C) Ujjain",
        "D) Bhopal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "<strong>Answer: B - Gwalior</strong>",
      "id": "zbev6gr"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "5. Raja Bhoj, who built the Bhojtal (Upper Lake) at Bhopal, belonged to which dynasty?",
      "id": "bchk4th"
    },
    {
      "id": "op4bgdw",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "A) Chandela",
        "B) Gond",
        "C) Paramara",
        "D) Tomar"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "<strong>Answer: C - Paramara dynasty</strong>",
      "id": "qp9xryr"
    },
    {
      "id": "2xxv9fd",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "12.2 Multiple Choice Questions – Geography"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "6. The highest peak of Madhya Pradesh is:",
      "id": "x8er2w4"
    },
    {
      "id": "kn3lajz",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "A) Amarkantak",
        "B) Dhupgarh",
        "C) Janapav",
        "D) Tamia"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "<strong>Answer: B - Dhupgarh (1350m), Pachmarhi</strong>",
      "id": "qnmf9di"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "7. The Narmada River originates from:",
      "id": "038vds4"
    },
    {
      "id": "7zccbl2",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "A) Pachmarhi",
        "B) Betul",
        "C) Amarkantak",
        "D) Janapav"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "<strong>Answer: C - Amarkantak (Anuppur district)</strong>",
      "id": "zobualu"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "8. Madhya Pradesh is called the 'Tiger State of India' because it has:",
      "id": "b9hi0ze"
    },
    {
      "id": "35hx8zo",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "A) Largest tiger reserve area",
        "B) Highest number of tigers",
        "C) First tiger reserve in India",
        "D) First White Tiger"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "<strong>Answer: B - Highest number of tigers in India</strong>",
      "id": "cud02hp"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "9. Malanjkhand in Balaghat district is famous for:",
      "id": "7d1s4i8"
    },
    {
      "id": "9g2a44p",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "A) Diamond mining",
        "B) Gold mining",
        "C) Copper mining",
        "D) Coal mining"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "<strong>Answer: C - Copper mining (Largest copper mine in Asia)</strong>",
      "id": "e3s08y2"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "10. The Chambal Wildlife Sanctuary is primarily known for protection of:",
      "id": "ebkyoyp"
    },
    {
      "id": "b714kzx",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "A) Bengal Tiger",
        "B) Barasingha",
        "C) Indian Gharial",
        "D) Asiatic Lion"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "<strong>Answer: C - Indian Gharial (also river dolphin and crocodile)</strong>",
      "id": "mmnkpnc"
    },
    {
      "id": "vzcirmc",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "12.3 Multiple Choice Questions – Culture and Miscellaneous"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "11. The Bhagoria Haat festival is associated with which tribe?",
      "id": "39oah38"
    },
    {
      "id": "75sxe6n",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "A) Gond",
        "B) Bhil and Bhilala",
        "C) Baiga",
        "D) Korku"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "<strong>Answer: B - Bhil and Bhilala (Jhabua, Alirajpur)</strong>",
      "id": "1y1o0pu"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "12. Maheshwari Sarees are woven in:",
      "id": "p1dfvfv"
    },
    {
      "id": "4g1mv94",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "A) Chanderi, Ashoknagar",
        "B) Maheshwar, Khargone",
        "C) Bagh, Dhar",
        "D) Ujjain"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "<strong>Answer: B - Maheshwar, Khargone district</strong>",
      "id": "iu00a7t"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "13. The first white tiger in modern history was discovered in which district of MP?",
      "id": "zen725z"
    },
    {
      "id": "7svitka",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "A) Mandla",
        "B) Umaria",
        "C) Rewa",
        "D) Balaghat"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "<strong>Answer: C - Rewa (by Maharaja Martand Singh in 1951)</strong>",
      "id": "588pxw8"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "14. Simhastha (Kumbh Mela at Ujjain) is held every:",
      "id": "8q33qrg"
    },
    {
      "id": "uk9xuud",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "A) 6 years",
        "B) 12 years",
        "C) 4 years",
        "D) 3 years"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "<strong>Answer: B - Every 12 years</strong>",
      "id": "xnjnk2e"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "15. The Bhopal Gas Tragedy occurred in the year:",
      "id": "h4n30vi"
    },
    {
      "id": "jbt5ict",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "A) 1982",
        "B) 1984",
        "C) 1986",
        "D) 1988"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "<strong>Answer: B - 1984 (night of 2-3 December)</strong>",
      "id": "k5r3r4k"
    }
  ],
  "enriched": false
}